# Binance Market Intelligence Bot — environment variables
#
# Binance market data itself never needs an API key/secret — that part
# works with zero environment variables, in dev and on Vercel alike.
# Everything below is OPTIONAL and additive. See README for the full
# "Supabase setup" and "Alerts that work with the browser closed" guides.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Supabase (persistence synced across devices, instead of per-browser
#    IndexedDB). Safe to expose to the browser — these are the project URL
#    and the RLS-restricted "anon" key, never a service-role key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only. Bypasses Row Level Security — required ONLY for the cron
# alert job to read every opted-in user's watchlist/config and dedupe
# notifications. NEVER prefix this NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit it, never
# use it in a route that acts on a single browser's request.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Web Push (native OS/browser notifications, delivered even with no tab
#    open). Generate your own pair — never reuse an example key pair:
#       node scripts/generate-vapid-keys.mjs
#    Requires Supabase (push subscriptions are stored server-side so the
#    cron job can reach them with nobody looking at the app).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Background alert scanner (app/api/cron/scan) — the part that notifies
#    you even with the browser fully closed. Something OUTSIDE your browser
#    must call this route on a schedule: Vercel Cron (once/day on the free
#    Hobby plan — see README), a free external scheduler like cron-job.org,
#    or the included GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/scan.yml,
#    every 5 min, free). Whatever calls it must send this secret back,
#    either as header `x-cron-secret: <value>` or `?secret=<value>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=

# Single-tenant fallback path: works with ZERO Supabase setup. Comma-
# separated symbols, Telegram bot token + chat id (see @BotFather), and/or
# a webhook URL. Leave CRON_SYMBOLS empty to disable this path entirely
# (e.g. if you're relying solely on the Supabase multi-user path below).
CRON_SYMBOLS=BTCUSDT,ETHUSDT,SOLUSDT,BNBUSDT
CRON_MIN_SCORE=80
CRON_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
CRON_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
CRON_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Multi-user path (requires SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY above): bounds how
# much work one cron invocation does, to stay inside your Vercel plan's
# function-duration limit.
CRON_MAX_USERS=25
CRON_MAX_SYMBOLS_PER_USER=8
